Chapter: IdentityCapGate

 The child reports its inherited identity and its parent's identity
 over a kernel channel, then the parent restricts the child's identity
 bit. Channels and spawning are Concurrent, identity-set is Identity,
 process-restrict-cap is Capability — the opening declares all three
 plus Console.

Section: Body
  send-second : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Concurrent] Integer
  send-second (ch) (b) (first) = chan-kern-send ch b

  child-body : Integer, Integer -> [Concurrent] Integer
  child-body (ch) (x) =
    send-second ch (identity-get-proc 0 0) (chan-kern-send ch (identity-whoami 0))

  recv-after-wait : Integer, Integer -> [Concurrent] Integer
  recv-after-wait (ch) (child) =
    let wt = process-wait child
    in chan-kern-recv ch

  gate-verdict : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  gate-verdict (child-id) (reported-parent) (restrict-id) (parent-id) =
    if child-id /= parent-id then "FAIL: child identity wrong"
    else if reported-parent /= parent-id then "FAIL: child saw wrong parent id"
    else if restrict-id /= 0 then "FAIL: restrict failed"
    else "PASS"

  opening : [Console, Identity, Concurrent, Capability] Nothing = act
    ch <- chan-kern-create 4
    s <- identity-set 0 hardware-random
    child <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body ch x)
    restrict-id <- process-restrict-cap child 15
    child-id <- recv-after-wait ch child
    reported <- chan-kern-recv ch
    print-line-uni (gate-verdict child-id reported restrict-id (identity-whoami 0))
  end
